<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Borobudur</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Borobudur is a monumental <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahayana-buddhism">Mahayana</a> Buddhist temple in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>, built in the eighth and ninth centuries under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sailendra-dynasty">Sailendra dynasty</a>. It is one of the largest Buddhist monuments in the world, decorated with extensive relief carvings. Because the Sailendras were closely connected to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya</a>, the site cites Borobudur as a sign of the Srivijaya Empire's cultural and political influence across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java-sea">Java Sea</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/borobudur.jpg" alt="Borobudur" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Heri nugroho · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pradaksina.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
